From 36912738360d8f90a30e77744d027a4505b90ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:16:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cityman: keep the Adreno GPU and its SMMU
 disabled

Part of the reference project used: msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts (&gpu okay) and the SAFE DT
(&gpu, &gpu_iommu disabled), qcom_iommu.c attach path.
Before: with GX collapsed the GPU SMMU resume fails (gfx3d clock stuck off), qcom_iommu_attach_dev() ignores
that and programs the context bank anyway; on 2026-11-09 every FULL DT boot reset right after
'fdb00000.gpu: Adding to iommu group 0' (~26.6 s), while the SAFE DT, which disables both, always booted.
The GPU did not work anyway (no GX rail described). Display (MDP/DSI) is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: chaoso85 <216391968+chaoso85@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts    | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
index 92f88d1f00b..e86245ca38b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8994-msft-lumia-octagon-cityman.dts
@@ -55,8 +55,20 @@ F0 11 30 03 00 00 00 0C
 	];
 };
 
+/*
+ * Adreno 430 and its SMMU stay off until the GX rail (adreno vdd/vddcx) is described:
+ * with GX collapsed OXILI_GFX3D_CLK never turns on, qcom_iommu_resume() fails, and
+ * qcom_iommu_attach_dev() ignores that and programs the GPU SMMU context bank anyway.
+ * On 2026-11-09 every boot reset right there (26.65 s, "fdb00000.gpu: Adding to iommu
+ * group 0"), while the SAFE DT (GPU + GPU SMMU disabled) always booted. Display (MDP/DSI)
+ * does not need the GPU.
+ */
 &gpu {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&gpu_iommu {
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &mdss {
-- 
